{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISIONS — recorded before acting on them.\n\n1. HOLD 0d76 OPEN until Bedrock is CONFIRMED to clear the bar. It does not close as \"measured, bar not\n   cleared\". The story's obligation is a confirmed verdict, not merely a measured one.\n\n2. HOLD THE CUTOVER (eb6e / S8) on the same condition. Cutover is AUTHORIZED IN PRINCIPLE once there\n   are no known bugs in the Bedrock implementation — and on that narrow point the condition is already\n   met: every open bug in this epic is in the parity HARNESS (62ac, 635f) or in provider-agnostic\n   caching (f81d, e3cd), not in the Bedrock provider code. The Bedrock implementation bugs 03b0 and\n   7b22 are closed. What blocks cutover is therefore the bar confirmation, not a Bedrock defect.\n\n3. NO ANTHROPIC-vs-ANTHROPIC NOISE-FLOOR RUN. Further expensive evals require justification beyond\n   caution or establishing a floor, and that control was justified on exactly those grounds. It is not\n   approved. NOTE THE CONSEQUENCE HONESTLY: without it we cannot say whether \"zero decision flips\" is\n   achievable by ANY provider pair, including Anthropic against itself. If the corrected re-score still\n   fails on flips, that unknown is the reason a confirmation may be unreachable by measurement alone,\n   and the bar itself would need revisiting rather than another run.\n\nWHAT \"CONFIRMED\" NOW DEPENDS ON, in order:\n  a. 62ac (false-accept metric inverted) and 635f (errored pairs scored as flips) are being fixed now.\n     Both are root-caused and operator-approved.\n  b. The already-recorded live run is then RE-SCORED OFFLINE with the corrected metrics — zero model\n     calls, zero spend. The recorded results live at\n     `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json`, 30 per-case records per slot.\n  c. If the corrected verdict clears the bar, Bedrock is confirmed and the cutover unblocks.\n     If it does not, the remaining failures get root-caused (/rebar-debug is approved for that), and\n     the question returns to the operator with evidence rather than another expensive run.\n\nSTANDING FACTS the next session should not re-derive:\n* All three observed decision flips are GENUINE, not errored-pair artefacts — error rate 0.000 on all\n  four arms and every flipped pair is errored=False, valid=True on BOTH sides.\n* All three flips FAVOUR Bedrock: standard caught a gold-BLOCK Anthropic missed; frontier declined to\n  fire on two gold-ADVISORY cases Anthropic false-fired on.\n* The frontier false-accept \"failure\" is an artefact of the inverted metric — Bedrock scored 0.786 ->\n  0.929, i.e. it false-fired LESS, and the harness penalised the improvement.\n* The parity run cost ~1,400 provider requests / ~15.4M input tokens against a plan that asserted at\n  most 360 model calls. A budget guard was considered and DEFERRED: useful during high-use development,\n  not in production, and not on the epic's critical path."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785720708066138001,"uuid":"62a9c745-afa6-48b0-afa9-6331e72d1275"}